Blue Bloods fans were stunned earlier  this fall and the show and ceremoniously  killed off one of its main characters  especially since the actress had touted  the show just two months before every  bit as it turns out the cast was reeling  just as much as everyone else the show's  actors recently spoke out on the  departure of Amy Carlson who's Linda  Reagan was revealed to be dead in the  season 8 premiere revealing their shock  and disappointment with the characters  abrupt demise Linda died off screen with  the show revealing in its return that a  character had been killed in a  helicopter crash two months earlier  after her exit Colson wrote a note of  thanks for fans who had supported her  throughout the series although she said  she was grateful to the cast and crew  deadline reports that there may have  been some trouble behind the scenes with  Colson reportedly deciding it was quote  time to move on after fulfilling her  contract while Linda's death was hard on  fans it was also especially hard on the  character's husband Danny played by  Donnie Wahlberg Wahlberg said he didn't  have to stray far from the truth to play  the grieving widower he told the crowd  at PaleyFest in New York rather than  tried to act or find something to do I  just thought about my friend Amy Carlson  I thought about all the years together  and all the highs and lows and the ups  and downs on the journey any tears I  shed in that scene was really Donnie  shedding them for Amy hopefully his  family of our cast the show and the  viewers will all mourn the loss together  and move forward after the season some  of Wahlberg's other co-stars also  expressed their sadness a Coulson's  decision to leave the show Sammy Gale  told TV Line Amy made the decision to  leave but we adore her we're very sad  she left Marisa Ramirez who plays  Danny's partner Detective Maria Baez  thinks the departure will prove  interesting for the show because Danny  will now need to turn to her support  adding we'll see if he takes it because  he's very very stubborn meanwhile her  co-star Bridget Moynahan added that she  was disappointed to learn that the  actress was departing saying it was  unfortunate that she made that decision  at the end of season seven so we were  stuck with the storyline as we could get  it but I'm really thrilled for her to go  off and pursue other things and follow  what she felt was best for her Carlson  for her parts wrote on Twitter that she  was appalled and sad about the comments  made at PaleyFest saying I love the show  cast and playing her why are y'all  looking at me thanks for watching click  the loop icon to subscribe to our  YouTube channel plus check out all this  cool stuff we know your love to  [Music]
 

